+# Privacy by design notes
+
+## Data minimization
+- The site is static and collects no personal data: no cookies, storage, analytics, or forms.
+- The server (`server.js`) does not log IPs or user agents, and sets `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`.
+- Browser features that leak data or enable tracking are disabled via `Permissions-Policy`.
+- Any new feature that collects data must collect the minimum fields, state the purpose in
+  `privacy-policy.html`, and define a retention period.
+
+## Third-party audit (performed 2026-10-19)
+| Third party | Use | Decision |
+|---|---|---|
+| images.unsplash.com | Hero image (leaked visitor IP to a third party) | Removed; image self-hosted at `assets/hero.jpg` |
+| `statikk` via `pnpm dlx` | Dev static server, unpinned remote fetch at startup | Replaced by dependency-free `server.js` |
+
+No third-party scripts, fonts, or embeds remain. The CSP (`default-src 'none'`, `img-src 'self'`) blocks any
+newly added third-party resource, so adding one requires a deliberate policy change and a new audit entry here.
+
+## Secure data handling
+- HTTPS enforced via HSTS and `upgrade-insecure-requests` (terminate TLS in front of `server.js`).
+- Only allow-listed files are served (no source/config exposure); path traversal is rejected.
+- Only GET/HEAD are accepted; responses default to `Cache-Control: no-store`.
+
+## Security headers
+CSP, HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, COOP, CORP, COEP and
+X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies are set in `server.js`. If deploying behind another host/CDN, replicate them there.
